{
  "case_id": "2019-18-587",
  "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2017, the Fifth Circuit held that DAPA and the expansion of DACA were likely unlawful, a judgment this Court affirmed by an equally divided Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Homeland Security",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Department of Homeland Security reasonably determined that it no longer wished to retain the DACA policy based on its belief that the policy was illegal, its serious doubts about its illegality, and its general opposition to broad non-enforcement policies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: General Francisco, there's a strange element to your argument because you're arguing this is a discretionary matter; it's not reviewable because it's committed to agency discretion. But, on the other hand, you say the agency had no discretion because this program was illegal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there's no argument by anybody or any possible argument that could be made that somehow the INA restricts the Department of Homeland Security's authority to enforce the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "agency -- and I think I'm quoting from the case law -- completely failed to consider an important aspect of the question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could continue the same question because, look, the best statement of the law in my mind -- this is a very old principle -- again, was Justice Scalia's writing for the Court in Fox."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But don't you have to -- don't you have to set up some kind of categories? I mean, everybody agrees, what is that, how many, 11 million people?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I pick up on Justice Kagan's question earlier? Does the Nielsen memo ever say, even if DACA was lawful, I would still exercise my policy discretion to discontinue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Private Respondents",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government's termination of DACA triggered abrupt, tangible, adverse consequences and substantial disruptions in the lives of 700,000 individuals, their families, employers, communities, and Armed Forces."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Private Respondents",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "only the Attorney General's unexplained assertion that he had no discretion because DACA was an unconstitutional exercise of authority by the executive branch."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the five kilos is reduced to three. Would that be reviewable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson, I -- I think you've moved on to the merits, and I --I guess I'm still struggling with Justice Alito's question on -- on reviewability. Can you help me understand what is the limiting principle?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- I choose not to do this. Aren't the dynamics of what happens between Congress and the President dramatically different in those circumstances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-587",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6462e834951c2781b570be865b133f4f2b2736c67fb80dc0a6c73d1efb857c9f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6462e834951c-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In that penultimate paragraph, what is the shortfall in the discussion of reliance interests, in your view?"
    },
